WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.121 --> 00:00:02.454
(gun shots)

00:00:04.814 --> 00:00:06.692
- So we're here today
at Oak Tree Gun Club,

00:00:06.692 --> 00:00:08.505
and we're gonna shoot a bunch of stuff

00:00:08.505 --> 00:00:10.244
that you see utilized in movies,

00:00:10.244 --> 00:00:12.036
or that you just have around your house,

00:00:12.036 --> 00:00:14.073
to see what's actually bulletproof.

00:00:14.073 --> 00:00:16.473
Disclaimer: we're here with professionals

00:00:16.473 --> 00:00:17.657
in a safe environment.

00:00:17.657 --> 00:00:19.374
Do not try this at home.

00:00:19.374 --> 00:00:21.295
We're testing it for you.

00:00:21.295 --> 00:00:23.712
(rock music)

00:00:25.753 --> 00:00:27.859
- Today, we are going to be using the

00:00:27.859 --> 00:00:30.344
.22 long rifle round,
which is a lighter bullet

00:00:30.344 --> 00:00:31.880
that travels very fast.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.875
We're gonna be using a
nine millimeter Luger,

00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:36.243
and we are going to be using a

00:00:36.243 --> 00:00:38.195
.460 Smith and Wesson Magnum.

00:00:38.195 --> 00:00:39.635
- [Woman] What does the most damage?

00:00:39.635 --> 00:00:41.534
- [Robert] The .460, hands down.

00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:42.856
- 'Cause it's the biggest?

00:00:42.856 --> 00:00:45.224
- It's the longest casing with
the most powder behind it.

00:00:45.224 --> 00:00:46.739
It's also the heaviest bullet, so you get

00:00:46.739 --> 00:00:48.659
a lot of weight with a
lot of velocity behind it.

00:00:48.659 --> 00:00:51.496
95% of the stuff you
see in movies, it's...

00:00:51.496 --> 00:00:53.257
No.
- [Woman] It doesn't work?

00:00:53.257 --> 00:00:54.090
- It doesn't work.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.774
- They're a bunch of liars.
- For the most part.

00:00:55.774 --> 00:00:58.952
- The ol' frying pan flip trick.

00:00:58.952 --> 00:01:01.256
- We're gonna try and
shoot a cast iron skillet

00:01:01.256 --> 00:01:03.945
with a nine millimeter and
a .460 Smith and Wesson.

00:01:03.945 --> 00:01:05.854
- [Robert] I think the
.460's gonna go through it.

00:01:05.854 --> 00:01:07.902
- Kate's gonna go home without a skillet.

00:01:07.902 --> 00:01:09.480
(laughter)

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:10.313
Sorry!

00:01:12.104 --> 00:01:14.216
(gun firing)

00:01:14.216 --> 00:01:15.859
Oh! That went through!

00:01:15.859 --> 00:01:17.352
- Nope.
- What do you mean "No?"

00:01:17.352 --> 00:01:19.763
- Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah it did.

00:01:19.763 --> 00:01:22.180
(gun firing)

00:01:24.008 --> 00:01:26.846
- Two holes. We've got two holes.

00:01:26.846 --> 00:01:29.417
Nine millimeter hit it,
almost in a bull's eye.

00:01:29.417 --> 00:01:32.435
- I actually thought the
nine would bounce off of it.

00:01:32.435 --> 00:01:33.768
- It went right through.

00:01:33.768 --> 00:01:37.910
Turns out, cast iron
skillet: not a great shield.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:38.743
Noted.

00:01:38.743 --> 00:01:40.196
It's time to shoot an iPhone.

00:01:40.196 --> 00:01:42.852
We're gonna shoot it with
a nine millimeter gun.

00:01:42.852 --> 00:01:44.868
We've only got one shot.

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:47.285
(gun firing)

00:01:52.704 --> 00:01:55.095
The iPhone didn't survive.

00:01:55.095 --> 00:01:56.599
(laughter)

00:01:56.599 --> 00:01:58.924
The front doesn't look so bad.

00:01:58.924 --> 00:02:01.922
The back looks pretty terrible.

00:02:01.922 --> 00:02:04.428
We're gonna shoot a car door.

00:02:04.428 --> 00:02:08.011
My prediction is that
it will stop the .22.

00:02:08.855 --> 00:02:11.137
(gun firing)

00:02:11.137 --> 00:02:13.637
It looks like it went through.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:17.757
(gun firing)

00:02:18.593 --> 00:02:20.908
(gun firing)

00:02:20.908 --> 00:02:22.007
- Jesus Christ!

00:02:22.007 --> 00:02:26.273
- So this is the .22 hole,
that's the nine hole,

00:02:26.273 --> 00:02:28.216
and this is the .460?

00:02:28.216 --> 00:02:30.915
- The nine went through for sure.

00:02:30.915 --> 00:02:33.603
- The .22 also went through!

00:02:33.603 --> 00:02:38.335
That's crazy; all three of
them went through the door.

00:02:38.335 --> 00:02:39.995
Get out of your car!

00:02:39.995 --> 00:02:41.617
(laughter)

00:02:41.617 --> 00:02:43.782
- You guys wanna shoot the table?

00:02:43.782 --> 00:02:45.083
- [Man In Sweater] Yeah we do!

00:02:45.083 --> 00:02:46.662
(cheering)

00:02:46.662 --> 00:02:48.166
- So we're gonna shoot a table,

00:02:48.166 --> 00:02:49.723
because I feel like, in every movie,

00:02:49.723 --> 00:02:51.560
you always see people
hiding behind tables.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:54.810
And this time, we get to shoot the gun.

00:02:55.971 --> 00:02:57.210
- Go ahead and pick those up,

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:00.043
keep your fingers off the trigger.

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:03.482
Go ahead and watch your barrels,

00:03:03.482 --> 00:03:05.562
you're gonna take aim at that table.

00:03:05.562 --> 00:03:07.957
Everybody's got eyes and ears on?

00:03:07.957 --> 00:03:09.290
One, two, three.

00:03:10.243 --> 00:03:12.743
(guns firing)

00:03:17.528 --> 00:03:18.435
There we go.

00:03:18.435 --> 00:03:20.483
- Oh yeah, right through the top there.

00:03:20.483 --> 00:03:22.040
- That was Gustav.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.086
After all we've seen today,

00:03:23.086 --> 00:03:25.059
the chair's probably
not gonna stop a bullet,

00:03:25.059 --> 00:03:27.899
so we might as well just
put a bunch of them in it.

00:03:27.899 --> 00:03:28.806
Right?
- [Voiceover] Yep!

00:03:28.806 --> 00:03:29.639
- Yeah!

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:32.980
(guns firing)

00:03:35.974 --> 00:03:38.474
(guns firing)

00:03:46.896 --> 00:03:48.400
We just blew up the chair!

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.171
So guns work.

00:03:50.171 --> 00:03:53.190
What we learned today was
that guns do their jobs,

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.608
and movies are fake,

00:03:54.608 --> 00:03:57.904
but I feel like we
probably knew that already.

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.302
- But you don't need to squeeze the gun.

00:03:59.302 --> 00:04:00.742
I'm talking to you.

00:04:00.742 --> 00:04:02.320
- What?

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:04.891
I've got a very soft touch.
- Uh huh.

00:04:04.891 --> 00:04:06.140
Tell that to that Rav 4.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:07.210
(laughing)

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:11.293
You probably ripped it
right off the car, right?

